{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginpaywallreference"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"article","title":"SwiduxPaywall Reference","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}]},"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"type":"text","text":" is a domain plugin that owns the paywall slice of your app’s state and routes paywall actions through the Swidux dispatch cycle. It is provider-agnostic: the plugin knows nothing about RevenueCat, StoreKit, products, prices, or purchase results. You supply a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":" conformer that talks to whichever purchase backend you use, and the plugin manages presentation state, async progress, and entitlement transitions."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For end-to-end wiring, see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". For where this plugin sits in the lifecycle, see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Library target","type":"heading","anchor":"Library-target","level":2},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Product: "},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Import: ","type":"text"},{"code":"import SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Add the product to your target dependencies in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Package.swift"},{"type":"text","text":" alongside "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Provided implementations","type":"heading","anchor":"Provided-implementations","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin ships with two in-repo conformers, both provider-agnostic and SDK-free:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"MockPaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — fixed snapshot, stream finishes immediately; for previews and tests.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"SimulatedPaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — a stateful, fully driveable service. Paired with the "},{"code":"SwiduxDevPaywallUI","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" debug sheet, it lets a developer or QA tester grant Pro\/Trial\/Permanent, restore, and simulate failure\/latency — all flowing through the real plugin pipeline, with no SDK and no vendor commitment. Use it as the ","type":"text"},{"code":"service:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" while the paywall vendor decision is still open."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For production RevenueCat integrations, the "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/heirloomlogic\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall"},{"type":"text","text":" companion package provides:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RevenueCatPaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":" — a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":" conformer that bridges RevenueCat’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CustomerInfo"},{"type":"text","text":" stream and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"restorePurchases()"},{"type":"text","text":" API."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MockRevenueCatPaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":" — a RevenueCat-flavored mock for previews."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywallUI"},{"type":"text","text":" — a SwiftUI sheet built on RevenueCatUI that hands purchase results back through the plugin."}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For other backends (StoreKit, custom server), implement ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":" directly — see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" Step 3, Path B."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Types","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Types"},{"text":"`PaywallPlugin<RootState, RootAction>`","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"PaywallPlugin%3CRootState-RootAction%3E"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@MainActor"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPlugin"},{"text":" conformer. Owns a slice of root state typed as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallState"},{"text":" and an action enum typed as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallAction"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public init(","    state: WritableKeyPath<RootState, PaywallState>,","    action toRootAction: @escaping @Sendable (PaywallAction) -> RootAction,","    extractAction: @escaping @Sendable (RootAction) -> PaywallAction?,","    service: any PaywallService,","    openURL: @escaping @Sendable (URL) async -> Void = { \/* default *\/ }",")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default "},{"code":"openURL","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" handler calls "},{"code":"UIApplication.shared.open","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on UIKit and ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSWorkspace.shared.open","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on AppKit. Override it for testing or for non-standard environments.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"`PaywallState`","type":"heading","anchor":"PaywallState","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" struct. The slice the plugin owns.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public struct PaywallState: Sendable, Equatable {","    public var isPro: Bool","    public var hasPermanentLicense: Bool","    public var isPresented: Bool","    public var requestedReason: String?","    public var isLoading: Bool","    public var error: String?","    public var isCustomerCenterPresented: Bool","","    public init(","        isPro: Bool = false,","        hasPermanentLicense: Bool = false,","        isPresented: Bool = false,","        requestedReason: String? = nil,","        isLoading: Bool = false,","        error: String? = nil,","        isCustomerCenterPresented: Bool = false","    )","","    public var isGateSatisfied: Bool { isPro || hasPermanentLicense }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"isGateSatisfied","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the single read your feature code should consult before running gated work. It is ","type":"text"},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when the user holds an active pro subscription or a permanent license.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"`PaywallAction`","type":"heading","anchor":"PaywallAction","level":3},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public enum PaywallAction: Sendable {","    case request(reason: String)","    case dismiss","    case observeCustomerInfo","    case refreshCustomerInfo","    case customerInfoUpdated(EntitlementSnapshot)","    case refreshFailed(String)","    case restorePurchases","    case presentCustomerCenter","    case dismissCustomerCenter","    case openManageSubscriptions","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"`EntitlementSnapshot`","type":"heading","anchor":"EntitlementSnapshot","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Provider-agnostic value the service emits to describe the user’s current entitlement.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public struct EntitlementSnapshot: Sendable, Equatable {","    public let isPro: Bool","    public let hasPermanentLicense: Bool","","    public init(isPro: Bool = false, hasPermanentLicense: Bool = false)","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"`PaywallService` (protocol)","type":"heading","anchor":"PaywallService-protocol","level":3},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public protocol PaywallService: Sendable {","    func customerInfo() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot","    func customerInfoStream() -> AsyncStream<EntitlementSnapshot>","    func restorePurchases() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"`MockPaywallService`","type":"heading","anchor":"MockPaywallService","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Test\/preview conformer that returns a fixed snapshot. Its stream finishes immediately.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public struct MockPaywallService: PaywallService {","    public init(isPro: Bool = false, hasPermanentLicense: Bool = false)","    public func customerInfo() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot","    public func customerInfoStream() -> AsyncStream<EntitlementSnapshot>","    public func restorePurchases() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"`SimulatedPaywallService`","type":"heading","anchor":"SimulatedPaywallService","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Stateful ","type":"text"},{"code":"actor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformer for development and QA. Holds the current entitlement and multicasts changes through ","type":"text"},{"code":"customerInfoStream()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so simulated grants survive a later ","type":"text"},{"code":"refreshCustomerInfo","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"restorePurchases","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" exactly as a real service would.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public actor SimulatedPaywallService: PaywallService {","    public init(","        isPro: Bool = false,","        hasPermanentLicense: Bool = false,","        subsystem: String = \"Swidux\",","        category: String = \"Paywall\"","    )","","    \/\/ PaywallService: customerInfo \/ customerInfoStream \/ restorePurchases","","    \/\/ Simulation surface (not part of PaywallService — driven by the dev UI):","    public func grantPro()","    public func grantTrial()","    public func grantPermanentLicense()","    public func setFree()","    public func setRestoreShouldFail(_ shouldFail: Bool)","    public func setRefreshShouldFail(_ shouldFail: Bool)","    public func setArtificialDelay(_ delay: Duration)","}","","public enum SimulatedPaywallError: Error, Equatable {","    case restoreFailed","    case refreshFailed","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"EntitlementSnapshot","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" only models ","type":"text"},{"code":"isPro","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"hasPermanentLicense","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so ","type":"text"},{"code":"grantTrial()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" yields ","type":"text"},{"code":"isPro == true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and is distinguished from ","type":"text"},{"code":"grantPro()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" only in the log line.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"`SwiduxDevPaywallUI`","type":"heading","anchor":"SwiduxDevPaywallUI","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A separate, opt-in library product (","type":"text"},{"code":"import SwiduxDevPaywallUI","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") providing a bare-bones debug paywall sheet. It mirrors the shape of the vendor paywall UI so the call site is unchanged when a real provider is adopted:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["someView.devPaywall(","    state: store.paywall,","    service: simulatedPaywallService,","    onAction: { store.send(.paywall($0)) }",")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The sheet shows the live ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", grant buttons, real Restore\/Refresh flows, and QA failure\/latency toggles. On macOS the sheet uses a 400×600 minimum, matching the vendor paywall UI. Hold a ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"single"}]},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"SimulatedPaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instance and pass it to both ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store.configured()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (as the plugin’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"service:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") and ","type":"text"},{"code":".devPaywall(...)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["@State private var paywallService = SimulatedPaywallService()","@State private var store: AppStore","","init() {","    let service = SimulatedPaywallService()","    _paywallService = State(initialValue: service)","    _store = State(initialValue: .configured(paywallService: service))","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This is the one place a dev\/QA service is intentionally constructed outside ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store.configured()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", because the debug UI must drive the same instance the plugin observes. Swapping to a real provider removes the shared-instance wiring and the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxDevPaywallUI","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" import along with the two-line ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store.configured()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" change.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Action semantics","type":"heading","anchor":"Action-semantics","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each case below describes the state mutation the plugin performs and the effect (if any) it returns.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"`request(reason: String)`","type":"heading","anchor":"requestreason-String","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Sets ","type":"text"},{"code":"isPresented = true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and stores ","type":"text"},{"code":"requestedReason","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Returns no effect. Dispatch this when a feature needs to gate behind a purchase.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"`dismiss`","type":"heading","anchor":"dismiss","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Sets ","type":"text"},{"code":"isPresented = false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and clears ","type":"text"},{"code":"requestedReason","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Returns an effect that dispatches ","type":"text"},{"code":".refreshCustomerInfo","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" so the entitlement is reconciled after the sheet closes (the user may have purchased while the sheet was up).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"`observeCustomerInfo`","type":"heading","anchor":"observeCustomerInfo","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Returns a long-lived effect that consumes ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallService.customerInfoStream()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and dispatches ","type":"text"},{"code":".customerInfoUpdated","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for every snapshot. Dispatch once on app launch (typically from a ","type":"text"},{"code":".task","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on the root view). The effect lives for the duration of the stream.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"`refreshCustomerInfo`","type":"heading","anchor":"refreshCustomerInfo","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Sets ","type":"text"},{"code":"isLoading = true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Returns a one-shot effect that calls ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallService.customerInfo()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and dispatches ","type":"text"},{"code":".customerInfoUpdated","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on success or ","type":"text"},{"code":".refreshFailed","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on error.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"`customerInfoUpdated(EntitlementSnapshot)`","type":"heading","anchor":"customerInfoUpdatedEntitlementSnapshot","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Sets ","type":"text"},{"code":"isPro","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"hasPermanentLicense","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from the snapshot, clears ","type":"text"},{"code":"isLoading","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and clears ","type":"text"},{"code":"error","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Returns no effect. The plugin emits this internally; your code rarely dispatches it directly. Note that the plugin emits this on ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"every"}]},{"text":" snapshot (each ","type":"text"},{"code":"customerInfoStream()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value, every ","type":"text"},{"code":"refreshCustomerInfo","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"restorePurchases","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), not only on entitlement changes — observe ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (or a value derived from it) for transitions rather than mapping this action directly. See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture#Service-Result-Actions-and-Transition-Observation","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"`refreshFailed(String)`","type":"heading","anchor":"refreshFailedString","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Sets ","type":"text"},{"code":"error","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to the given message and clears ","type":"text"},{"code":"isLoading","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Returns no effect.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"`restorePurchases`","type":"heading","anchor":"restorePurchases","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Sets ","type":"text"},{"code":"isLoading = true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Returns a one-shot effect that calls ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallService.restorePurchases()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and dispatches ","type":"text"},{"code":".customerInfoUpdated","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on success or ","type":"text"},{"code":".refreshFailed","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on error.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"`presentCustomerCenter` \/ `dismissCustomerCenter`","type":"heading","anchor":"presentCustomerCenter--dismissCustomerCenter","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Toggle ","type":"text"},{"code":"isCustomerCenterPresented","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". No effects. Bind these to a separate sheet if your purchase backend exposes a customer-center UI (RevenueCat does).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"`openManageSubscriptions`","type":"heading","anchor":"openManageSubscriptions","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Returns an effect that opens ","type":"text"},{"code":"itms-apps:\/\/apps.apple.com\/account\/subscriptions","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" via the configured ","type":"text"},{"code":"openURL","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" handler. This deep-links into the Settings → Subscriptions page on iOS and the equivalent on macOS.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Implementing a `PaywallService`","type":"heading","anchor":"Implementing-a-PaywallService","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin is purchase-agnostic. It does not know about products, prices, transactions, or vendor SDKs. Your conformer is responsible for translating whatever a backend reports into an ","type":"text"},{"code":"EntitlementSnapshot","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The protocol has three methods:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"customerInfo() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot"}]},{"text":" — One-shot fetch of the current entitlement. The plugin calls this from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".refreshCustomerInfo"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"customerInfoStream() -> AsyncStream<EntitlementSnapshot>"}]},{"text":" — Long-lived stream that yields every time the entitlement changes (purchase completes, subscription expires, family sharing update, etc.). The plugin consumes it from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".observeCustomerInfo"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"restorePurchases() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot"}]},{"text":" — Performs a restore against the user’s account and returns the resulting entitlement.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Note what the protocol does ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}]},{"text":" require: no product list, no purchase method, no receipt validation. Purchases happen inside whichever paywall UI you present (a RevenueCat paywall view, your own StoreKit-backed sheet, etc.). The plugin only cares about the entitlement that results.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A typical RevenueCat conformer holds a reference to the SDK and bridges its delegate or async APIs into ","type":"text"},{"code":"EntitlementSnapshot","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" values. A vanilla StoreKit conformer iterates ","type":"text"},{"code":"Transaction.currentEntitlements","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and listens to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Transaction.updates","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Either way, the plugin stays the same.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"API reference for the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" library — paywall presentation, entitlement observation, and purchase orchestration.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","anchor":"Related-Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"]},{"title":"Reference","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted"],"anchor":"Reference"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/GettingStarted":{"title":"Getting Started with Swidux","role":"article","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/gettingstarted","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add Swidux to your project and wire up unidirectional data flow with automatic persistence."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/MacrosReference":{"title":"Macros","role":"article","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/macrosreference","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Reference for ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Slice","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (the observation bridge between value-type state and SwiftUI), and for ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"text":" and its property markers (the SwiftData persistence bridge, shipped in ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginParentalGateReference":{"title":"SwiduxParentalGate Reference","role":"article","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginparentalgatereference","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API surface for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxParentalGate"},{"type":"text","text":" library — a domain plugin that guards actions behind a math challenge."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginAnalyticsReference":{"title":"SwiduxAnalytics Reference","role":"article","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginanalyticsreference","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"API reference for the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxAnalytics"},{"type":"text","text":" library — provider-agnostic analytics with declarative event mapping, auto-identify, and explicit dispatch for the cases the mapper can’t cover."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStoreGuide":{"title":"EntityStore","role":"article","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystoreguide","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection with built-in change tracking."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginArchitecture#Service-Result-Actions-and-Transition-Observation":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture#Service-Result-Actions-and-Transition-Observation","abstract":[],"kind":"section","title":"Service-Result Actions and Transition Observation","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture#Service-Result-Actions-and-Transition-Observation","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"type":"topic","title":"Swidux","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAPaywall":{"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddapaywall","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin into a Swidux app to gate features behind a subscription or lifetime purchase."}],"title":"Add a Paywall","type":"topic","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginKillswitchReference":{"title":"SwiduxKillswitch Reference","role":"article","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginkillswitchreference","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Public API surface for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxKillswitch"},{"type":"text","text":" library — the plugin, its state and actions, the service abstraction, and the version-comparison primitives."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide":{"title":"Persistence Middleware","role":"article","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistencemiddlewareguide","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Configure automatic persistence that drains entity changes and batches database writes."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginFeatureFlagsReference":{"type":"topic","title":"SwiduxFeatureFlags Reference","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags"},{"type":"text","text":" library — typed feature flags, A\/B variants, and remote-tunable scalar values backed by a Swidux-defined JSON wire format."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginfeatureflagsreference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"title":"UndoPlugin","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},"https://github.com/heirloomlogic/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall":{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/heirloomlogic\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall","title":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall","titleInlineContent":[{"code":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"link","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/heirloomlogic\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoRedo":{"title":"Undo \/ Redo","role":"article","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoredo","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add stack-based undo\/redo to your app with "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/KeyValueStoreGuide":{"title":"KeyValueStore","role":"collectionGroup","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/keyvaluestoreguide","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Persist scalar preferences like theme, sort order, or last-seen version — testably, with type-safe keys."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginArchitecture":{"type":"topic","title":"Plugin Architecture","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"}}}